  "body": {
    "id": "thm:fixed-protocol-generated-residual-expansion-impossible",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "No jointly valid construction with the properties in the question exists for the fixed class \\(\\mathcal A_n^{\\mathrm{LP}}\\) and the fixed handle \\(\\mathfrak H_{\\mathrm{orth}}(\\mathcal A_n^{\\mathrm{LP}})\\). More precisely, there are a law \\(P^\\circ\\in\\mathcal M_1(\\beta,L,c_0,C_0)\\) and a number \\(\\delta\\in(0,1-\\log 2)\\) such that, for every finite \\(C_m>0\\) and the unique admissible fit \\(\\widehat m\\in\\mathcal A_n^{\\mathrm{LP}}\\),\n\\[\n\\liminf_{n\\to\\infty}P^{\\circ\\otimes n}\\!\\left\\{\\mathcal G_n(1;C_m,\\widehat m)^c\\right\\}\n\\ge e^{-\\delta}>2e^{-1}.\n\\]\nConsequently, there are no constants \\(c_u,C_H,C_R,C_m>0\\), measurable statistics \\((\\widehat H^\\perp_{j,b}(\\widehat m):(j,b)\\in\\mathcal Q_d)\\), and associated data-dependent radii produced within \\(\\mathfrak H_{\\mathrm{orth}}(\\mathcal A_n^{\\mathrm{LP}})\\) for which, uniformly over \\(P\\in\\mathcal M_d(\\beta,L,c_0,C_0)\\), every \\(x\\ge1\\) with \\(u=x+\\log(2d)\\le c_u n\\) satisfies\n\\[\nP^{\\otimes n}\\!\\left(\n\\mathcal G_n(x;C_m,\\widehat m)^c\n\\cup\n\\left\\{\\exists(j,b)\\in\\mathcal Q_d:\n\\left|\\widehat H^\\perp_{j,b}(\\widehat m)-H_{j,b}\\right|\n>C_H\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{H_{j,b}u}{n}}+\\frac{u}{n}+r_n^4\\right)\n\\right\\}\n\\right)\n\\le 2e^{-x}.\n\\]\nIn particular, the complete package requested in the question, including the fourth-order nuisance remainder and joint null-interval coverage, is impossible under this fixed protocol. This result does not rule out other regression estimators, other independence statistics, or other residual-HSIC procedures.",
