    "proof_tex": "Theorem \\(\\mathrm{thm:fixed\\text{-}local\\text{-}polynomial\\text{-}uniform\\text{-}expansion\\text{-}impossible}\\) supplies a fixed law \\(P^\\circ\\in\\mathcal M_1(\\beta,L,c_0,C_0)\\) and \\(\\delta\\in(0,1-\\log 2)\\) for which, for every finite \\(C_m>0\\) and the unique fit \\(\\widehat m\\in\\mathcal A_n^{\\mathrm{LP}}\\),\n\\[\n\\liminf_{n\\to\\infty}P^{\\circ\\otimes n}\\!\\left\\{\\mathcal G_n(1;C_m,\\widehat m)^c\\right\\}\n\\ge e^{-\\delta}>2e^{-1}.\n\\]\nThe strict final inequality follows from \\(\\delta<1-\\log 2\\): exponentiation gives\n\\[\ne^{-\\delta}>e^{-(1-\\log 2)}=2e^{-1}.\n\\]\n\nSuppose, toward a contradiction, that the constants, statistics, and radii in the statement exist. Specialize their asserted uniform guarantee to the member law \\(P^\\circ\\), dimension \\(d=1\\), and \\(x=1\\). Then\n\\[\nu_1=1+\\log 2.\n\\]\nBecause \\(c_u>0\\), the required side condition \\(u_1\\le c_u n\\) holds for every integer \\(n\\ge \\lceil u_1/c_u\\rceil\\). For such \\(n\\), define the asserted failure event\n\\[\n\\mathcal F_n=\n\\mathcal G_n(1;C_m,\\widehat m)^c\n\\cup\n\\left\\{\\exists(1,b)\\in\\mathcal Q_1:\n\\left|\\widehat H^\\perp_{1,b}(\\widehat m)-H_{1,b}\\right|\n>C_H\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{H_{1,b}u_1}{n}}+\\frac{u_1}{n}+r_n^4\\right)\n\\right\\}.\n\\]\nBy construction of this union,\n\\[\n\\mathcal G_n(1;C_m,\\widehat m)^c\\subseteq\\mathcal F_n.\n\\]\nThe purported probability guarantee at \\(x=1\\) and monotonicity of probability therefore imply\n\\[\nP^{\\circ\\otimes n}\\!\\left\\{\\mathcal G_n(1;C_m,\\widehat m)^c\\right\\}\n\\le P^{\\circ\\otimes n}(\\mathcal F_n)\n\\le 2e^{-1}\n\\]\nfor all sufficiently large \\(n\\). Taking lower limits and invoking the witness bound yields the contradiction\n\\[\ne^{-\\delta}\n\\le\n\\liminf_{n\\to\\infty}P^{\\circ\\otimes n}\\!\\left\\{\\mathcal G_n(1;C_m,\\widehat m)^c\\right\\}\n\\le 2e^{-1}\n<e^{-\\delta}.\n\\]\nThus the requested simultaneous probability guarantee cannot hold. Since that guarantee is a necessary conjunct of the proposed construction, adding the stated derivative cancellation, fourth-order remainder bound, or null intervals cannot make the full package exist. The contradiction uses only the compulsory event \\(\\mathcal G_n\\) and the fixed admissible class \\(\\mathcal A_n^{\\mathrm{LP}}\\), which proves precisely the protocol-qualified negative conclusion and no broader impossibility claim.",
